==============================================================================
SELF-AUDIT CORRECTION + CONFOUND KILL (bridge step 0, same session)
==============================================================================
CONFOUND TESTED AND KILLED: peak-identity diagnostic through the switch
(C128_1e-4 viscous, OR_z128r384 inviscid): argmax fixed at the corner
(z*=0, r*=1.000) at every gated snapshot; wt_frac = 0.000 throughout
(omega_theta vanishes at the corner by symmetry; the |omega| max is the
swirl-gradient structure the whole time). No structure handoff -- the
sigma switch is a genuine direction-field change at ONE fixed structure.

CORRECTION (the "four e-folds" reading is RETRACTED): the amplitude axis
begins at 37.7 x A0 in every run because that IS the IC's corner
swirl-gradient amplitude (fixed geometric factor of the quartic shape;
early inviscid snapshots grow 37.7 -> 37.9, i.e. barely). The invariant,
restated honestly: THE SWITCH SITS AT A GROWTH FACTOR OF
54/37.7 = 1.43 (twelve-run spread 1.398-1.437, i.e. +-1.5%) ABOVE THE IC
CORNER-GRADIENT AMPLITUDE -- 0.36
e-folds, not 4. Everything plane-certified stands (A* proportional to
A0, nu-independent, both grids); the gloss inverts: the viscous
inversion switches on almost immediately in growth terms -- after less
than half an e-fold of corner-gradient amplification -- and then holds
at sigma ~ -1.2 for the entire observable collapse (a further ~1.5
e-folds in the gated windows). "Fixed dynamical age, four e-folds deep"
was wrong; "fixed 1.43x trigger, essentially at collapse onset" is what
the data says. Prior wordings in this file's READING section, EJA
#77/#78/#79 texts, and Token3 carry the old gloss; this entry corrects
them all.
